@owner: mason
@stability: stable
@since: 2026-06-09
@reviewed: 2026-10-15

Feature: Mason Root Command
  "Cobra root command wiring global flags and subcommands for the mason CLI."

  Provides:
    - cli.Execute @source("symbol:Execute")
    - cli.NewRootCommand @source("symbol:NewRootCommand")

  Invariants:
    - Persistent flags MUST be exactly --json, --yes, --quiet, --verbose, and --config; --dry-run belongs to deploy
    - --yes MUST only answer confirmations; it MUST NOT change which questions a command would otherwise ask
    - SilenceUsage and SilenceErrors MUST be true so cli controls error rendering

  OutOfScope:
    - Service orchestration and remote I/O (owned by subcommand handlers and internal packages)
    - Golden test fixtures (owned by cli test files)

  Scenario (happy-path): Help on bare invocation
    Given mason with no subcommand
    When the root command runs
    Then help is printed and exit is success

  Scenario (happy-path): Version subcommand
    Given mason version
    When the version command runs
    Then the mason version string is printed
